      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.The original test has several understandability issues: unused imports, an unused `WHITESPACE` constant, and assertions that lack context about why they're being checked. I'll write a cleaned-up version now.The improved test compiles successfully. The changes made were: removed all unused imports (`assertEquals` for strings, `assertThrows`, `assertTimeout`, `IntStream`, `ArrayUtils`, `StringUtils`, `Duration`) and the unused `WHITESPACE` constant, then added brief inline comments to each assertion explaining the intent — making it immediately clear why each reflective check on the constructor and class modifiers is present."
